---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { t } from '../../i18n/i18n.js';

const lang = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title={t('inami.meta.title', lang)}
  description={t('inami.meta.description', lang)}
  ogUrl="https://kajoble.com/en/inami"
>
  <div id="main" class="alt">
    <section id="one">
      <div class="inner">
        <header class="major">
          <h1>{t('inami.title', lang)}</h1>
        </header>
        <span class="image main"><img src="/images/inami-banner.jpg" alt="" /></span>
        <p>At INAMI, I contributed to the development of Practice Register, a large-scale platform designed to manage the careers, accreditation, and professional data of healthcare workers at the national level.</p>
        <p>In this role I:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Contributed to building a high-volume, mission-critical platform used by healthcare professionals and public institutions.</li>
          <li>Designed and optimized the database architecture, improving database team efficiency by 30% through clearer data models and performance improvements.</li>
          <li>Worked closely with UX/UI designers, streamlining collaboration workflows and reducing design-related effort by 50%, while ensuring a consistent and user-friendly interface.</li>
          <li>Actively contributed to code quality and reliability through automated testing and modern development practices.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The platform was built using C# (.NET 6), Blazor WebAssembly, Entity Framework, SQL, Keycloak for authentication, xUnit for testing, and Telerik UI components, respecting the constraints and quality standards of the healthcare and public sector.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
